    "background_story": "Dior, a struggling artist, found solace in the words of French poet Edmond Rostand. His plays, particularly 'Cyrano de Bergerac', inspired Dior to pursue his passion for writing. As a young man, Dior felt like an outcast, struggling to find his place in the world. But Rostand's works taught him that even the most unlikely heroes can make a lasting impact. Dior began to write his own poetry and plays, weaving tales of love, loss, and self-discovery. His unique voice and perspective eventually caught the attention of a prominent literary critic, who hailed him as a rising star in the literary world. Dior's success was a testament to the power of Rostand's words, which had ignited a fire within him to create and inspire others.",
